WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:07.834
Mr Saeed: Hello! Welcome to English Path. Unit one, lesson two. How are you?

2
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:14.911
Mr Saeed: Good morning, class! How are you today?

3
00:00:14.911 --> 00:00:16.964
Fahad: We're fine, thank you!

4
00:00:16.964 --> 00:00:21.343
Mr Saeed: Hello, Ali. How are you?

5
00:00:21.343 --> 00:00:24.381
Ali: I'm very well, thanks. And you?

6
00:00:24.381 --> 00:00:28.069
Mr Saeed: I'm OK, thank you. Sit down, please.

7
00:00:31.969 --> 00:00:34.243
Sara: How are you, Fahad?

8
00:00:34.243 --> 00:00:36.851
Fahad: Fine, thanks. And you?

9
00:00:36.851 --> 00:00:41.029
Sara: I'm OK, thanks. It's a lovely day today!

10
00:00:41.029 --> 00:00:44.148
Fahad: Yes, it is. Are you a new student?

11
00:00:44.148 --> 00:00:45.600
Sara: Yes, I am.

12
00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.021
Mr Saeed: Let's learn some new words.

13
00:00:51.021 --> 00:00:52.822
Mr Saeed: How are you?.

14
00:00:52.822 --> 00:00:54.487
Mr Saeed: fine.

15
00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:56.239
Mr Saeed: very well.

16
00:00:56.239 --> 00:00:57.796
Mr Saeed: thanks.

17
00:00:57.796 --> 00:00:59.369
Mr Saeed: OK.

18
00:00:59.369 --> 00:01:00.951
Mr Saeed: lovely.

19
00:01:00.951 --> 00:01:02.483
Mr Saeed: today.

20
00:01:02.483 --> 00:01:03.923
Mr Saeed: day.

21
00:01:03.923 --> 00:01:05.241
Mr Saeed: and.

22
00:01:07.641 --> 00:01:13.345
Mr Saeed: Now, the verb to be. Am, is and are.

23
00:01:13.345 --> 00:01:16.592
Mr Saeed: I goes with am. I'm fine.

24
00:01:16.592 --> 00:01:23.051
Mr Saeed: You, we and they go with are. How are you?

25
00:01:23.051 --> 00:01:28.308
Mr Saeed: He, she and it go with is. It's a lovely day.

26
00:01:28.308 --> 00:01:33.995
Mr Saeed: I = am · he / she / it = is · you / we / they = are

27
00:01:36.795 --> 00:01:40.796
Mr Saeed: In speaking, we use short forms.

28
00:01:40.796 --> 00:01:44.839
Mr Saeed: I am. I'm.

29
00:01:44.839 --> 00:01:47.778
Mr Saeed: You are. You're.

30
00:01:47.778 --> 00:01:50.910
Mr Saeed: He is. He's.

31
00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:54.084
Mr Saeed: It is. It's.

32
00:01:56.884 --> 00:02:00.987
Mr Saeed: Use how are you to ask about a person.
كيف حالك؟

33
00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:05.236
Mr Saeed: You can answer: I'm fine, thanks.

34
00:02:05.236 --> 00:02:08.794
Mr Saeed: Or: I'm very well, thank you.

35
00:02:08.794 --> 00:02:12.950
Mr Saeed: Or: I'm OK, thanks. Then ask: And you?

36
00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:20.634
Mr Saeed: Now, short answers. Use the same verb.

37
00:02:20.634 --> 00:02:24.570
Mr Saeed: Are you a student? Yes, I am.

38
00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:28.669
Mr Saeed: Is it a lovely day? Yes, it is.

39
00:02:28.669 --> 00:02:31.820
Mr Saeed: Is he your teacher? Yes, he is.

40
00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:37.155
Mr Saeed: Now, opposites.

41
00:02:37.155 --> 00:02:40.052
Mr Saeed: Morning. Evening.

42
00:02:40.052 --> 00:02:42.527
Mr Saeed: Good. Bad.

43
00:02:42.527 --> 00:02:45.217
Mr Saeed: Happy. Sad.

44
00:02:45.217 --> 00:02:47.167
Mr Saeed: Early. Late.

45
00:02:49.967 --> 00:02:52.589
Mr Saeed: Now listen and repeat.

46
00:02:52.589 --> 00:02:55.141
Mr Saeed: How are you?

47
00:02:57.041 --> 00:03:00.218
Mr Saeed: I'm fine, thanks.

48
00:03:02.118 --> 00:03:05.592
Mr Saeed: Very well, thank you.

49
00:03:07.492 --> 00:03:09.981
Mr Saeed: And you?

50
00:03:11.881 --> 00:03:13.815
Mr Saeed: It's a lovely day!

51
00:03:18.915 --> 00:03:22.148
Mr Saeed: Quick quiz! Choose the right word.

52
00:03:22.148 --> 00:03:27.006
Mr Saeed: How, blank, you? Are, or is?

53
00:03:29.306 --> 00:03:31.178
Fahad: How are you?

54
00:03:31.178 --> 00:03:37.585
Mr Saeed: I, blank, very well, thank you. Am, or are?

55
00:03:39.885 --> 00:03:42.157
Sara: I am very well.

56
00:03:42.157 --> 00:03:48.475
Mr Saeed: It, blank, a lovely day. Is, or are?

57
00:03:50.775 --> 00:03:52.958
Ali: It is a lovely day.

58
00:03:55.358 --> 00:04:00.459
Mr Saeed: Now it's your turn. Ask your partner: how are you? Then answer.

59
00:04:06.359 --> 00:04:09.900
Mr Saeed: Well done! See you in Lesson three.
